# Testing Rules

## General

Tests must verify behavior, not implementation details unnecessarily.

## Domain

Domain rules should be testable without:

- rendering;
- game engine;
- file system;
- network;
- UI.

## Determinism

Tests must prefer deterministic inputs.

Randomized game behavior must provide a way to control randomness
when deterministic testing is required.

## Regression

Existing tests must continue to pass.

Do not modify an existing test simply because the implementation
currently fails it.

First determine whether:

- the implementation is wrong;
- the test is outdated;
- the specification changed.

## Required validation

A task that introduces behavior should include appropriate tests.

At minimum verify:

- happy path;
- important boundary;
- invalid state where applicable.

## Integration

Integration tests should validate interaction between components.

Do not replace all unit tests with integration tests.